  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 bunch Swiss chard\n1 small bunch fresh dill"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, trim, and medium dice beets. Place in a 6-quart electric pressure cooker insert.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Fold chard leaves in half lengthwise, then slice off the stems. Cut leaves and stems into bite-sized pieces, keeping them separate. Place leaves in a medium bowl and set aside. Add stems to the pressure cooker.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Shave dill leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Add half to the pressure cooker (reserve remaining dill for serving).\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel, halve, and medium dice onion. Add to the pressure cooker along with beef, broth, and spices, then stir to combine the soup. Lock lid and set to pressure cook on HIGH for 15 minutes. ",
      "secondary_message": "1 medium yellow onion\n680 g beef for stew\n2 ½ cups beef broth\n1 tsp caraway seeds\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the soup is done, allow the pressure to release naturally for 10 minutes, then manually release any remaining pressure and open the lid. Change pressure to sauté on HIGH, then add Swiss chard leaves and vinegar to the insert. Stir to combine, then continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until greens are tender and soup is warmed through, 1-2 minutes more. Turn off heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp red wine vinegar"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, toast bread if desired, then spread with butter and cut in half. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 slice rye bread\n2 tbsp butter, unsalted"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide soup between bowls, then top with reserved dill and sour cream. Serve with buttered bread on the side and enjoy! \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup sour cream"
    }
  ],
